 ## Overview
 Quadratic Spline Splatting replaces the standard Gaussian reconstruction kernel with a quadratic spline function to improve rendering accuracy, particularly under perspective projection [S1, unofficial].
-
 ## How it works
 Quadratic Spline Splatting follows the general splatting pipeline defined in [Polynomial and Spline Kernels](9995-polynomial-and-spline-kernels.md), with the specific modification of the kernel function $h$ [G].
-
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** Volumetric data defined by voxel positions $\mathbf{p}_k$, density values $\rho_k$, and a quadratic spline kernel $h_{quad}$ [G].
+*   **Input:** Volumetric data defined by voxel positions $\mathbf{p}_k$, density values $\rho_k$, and a quadratic spline kernel $h_{\text{quad}}$ [G].
 *   **Output:** A 2D image where pixel intensities are computed by projecting the splatted quadratic splines [G].
-
 **Data Structures:**
-The method relies on standard splatting data structures. To accelerate rendering, view-dependent footprints are mapped to a generic footprint table computed once, or splats are represented as textures mapped to polygons rendered via texture mapping hardware [S1, unofficial].
